---
functor: 1
title: Blocks
---

set heading(numbering: none)

A block starts with `:::` and a kind, and ends with a line `:::`. Blocks can hold paragraphs, math, lists and other blocks.

```fn
::: theorem {#thm:main title="Closed work"}
If $F = nabla phi$, then the work around a loop is zero.
:::
```

# Kinds

| Kind | Number | Use |
|:--|:--|:--|
| `theorem` | yes | a main result |
| `lemma` | yes | a step to a result |
| `corollary` | yes | a result that follows |
| `proposition` | yes | a smaller result |
| `definition` | yes | a new term |
| `example` | yes | an example |
| `remark` | yes | a comment |
| `proof` | no | a proof, with an end mark |
| `note` | no | a side note |
| `figure` | own count | an image or a table with a caption |
| `quote` | no | a quotation |

The numbered kinds share one count: Theorem 1, Lemma 2, Definition 3.

# Options

| Option | Example | Result |
|:--|:--|:--|
| label | `{#thm:main}` | `@thm:main` shows "Theorem 1" |
| `title` | `title="Closed work"` | a name after the number |
| `width` | `width="60%"` | the width of a figure |

# One example of each kind

```fn
::: lemma {#lem:a}
Text.
:::

::: corollary
Text.
:::

::: proposition
Text.
:::

::: definition {#def:est title="Estimate"}
An estimate of $theta$ is $theta.hat$.
:::

::: example
Text.
:::

::: remark
Text.
:::

::: proof
Use @lem:a.
:::

::: note
Text.
:::

::: figure {#fig:plot width="60%"}
![A plot](plot.svg)
Caption: The plot of $f$.
:::

::: quote
Text.
:::
```

A figure needs a line `Caption: ...`. Without it, the compiler gives a warning.
